## Key finding (read before diagnosing any page)
- Site-wide impressions jumped about 2.2x on Nov 5 (134k to 302k a day) while clicks stayed flat (~550-720 a day). CTR fell from ~0.44% to ~0.22% and average position improved from ~4.2 to ~3.3.
- This points to a surge of non-clicking impressions (probably an image pack or AI surface; GSC cannot confirm). Head-term pages at position 1-3 with CTR under 0.1% are therefore likely a SERP-feature effect, not a title failure. Do not promise CTR lifts there; judge by clicks.
- Real clicks come from seasonal pages at positions 5-7. Among listed queries, seasonal queries give ~22% of clicks from ~8% of impressions.
- About half of all clicks (2,079 of 4,319) arrive through the Product snippets search appearance, at 0.82% CTR (position 6.23).
- Site-wide baseline (7 days): 1,872,246 impressions, 4,334 clicks, 0.23% CTR.

**Deadlines:** Thanksgiving Nov 26, Christmas Dec 25, New Year's Eve Dec 31. Title/CTR changes take ~1-3 weeks to show, content changes ~2-6 weeks, so Thanksgiving pages go first.

